Z||000000||msweldon||04-16-2001||09:11 AM||||Right now my 87gt is in storage in a relatives garage while I save up for my DOHC swap.  I usually take it out about once every 2 - 3 wks for about 30mins.  Last night while heading back in the gt, the clutch got "real" limp and it became increasingly difficult to get it into another gear.  I would have to double, if not triple or quadruple, clutch just to get it into gear.  <P>Is this part of the "infamous" fiero clutch problem.  If so, could someone point me in the right direction and I'll then scour the rest of the board, if not, any ideas or tips.<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Sincerely,<BR>Marc Weldon||||reg||1
Z||000001||NSUMEY||04-16-2001||09:33 AM||||I don't about your year...but my 84 was having alot of clutch trouble even after installing a new clutch....check out this site for info  <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>    he has an archive which has helped me solve my problem||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||04-16-2001||12:03 PM||||Sounds like you're losing clutch fluid.  My GT has a small leak somewhere (I think in the braided line), and my clutch started doing that.  Had to push it in 2 or 3 times, didn't take much to push it down.. looked in the resevoir and it was pretty much empty.  I just added some fluid and it was all back to normal, though.  Hope that's all it takes for yours.||||reg||1
